hub.com/celery/celery.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery","homepage":"https://docs.celeryq.dev","size":36397,"stargazers_count":28268,"watchers_count":28268,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4989,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":773,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["amqp","python","python-library","python3","queue-tasks","queue-workers","queued-jobs","redis","redis-queue","sqs","sqs-queue","task-manager","task-runner","task-scheduler"],"visibility":"public","forks":4989,"open_issues":773,"watchers":28268,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/pulls/10155","html_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/10155","diff_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/10155.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/pull/10155.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-01T09:37:52Z"},"body":"## Description\n\nThe existing documentation for `on_after_finalize` just says \"Signal sent after app has been finalized\" — which essentially repeats the signal name without explaining what \"finalized\" actually means. This is confusing for users trying to understand the app lifecycle (as reported in #7280).\n\nThis PR updates both the class attribute docstring in `celery/app/base.py` and the reference docs in `docs/reference/celery.rst` to explain that finalization:\n\n- Evaluates all pending task decorators\n- Loads built-in tasks\n- Binds every task to the app\n\nThis makes `on_after_finalize` the earliest point at which the full task registry is available, which is the key information users need when choosing between `on_after_configure` and `on_after_finalize`.\n\nFixes #7280","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/10155/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/10155/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/comments/3979267144","html_url":"https://github.com/celery/celery/issues/7280#issuecomment-3979267144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/celery/celery/issues/7280","id":3979267144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAALQjM7tLsxI","user":{"login":"Br1an67","id":29810238,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5ODEwMjM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29810238?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67","html_url":"https://github.com/Br1an67","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Br1an67/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T06:31:11Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T06:31:11Z","body":"I'd like to work on this. Updated the docstring and reference docs to explain that finalization evaluates pending task decorators, loads built-in tasks, and binds all tasks to the app — making it the earliest point where the full task registry is availa